 R←Test_Misc_007(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;folder;g;logFolder
⍝ Exercise `OpenAppLog`: the application log must end up in `[LOGGING]Folder`, with or without
⍝ a trailing separator there, and must not be created at all with `[LOGGING]Log = 0`.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 folder←∆GetTestFolder,'/Test_Misc_007'
 ##.Plodder.⎕SHADOW'F'                              ⍝ A local of `Run` in a running server,
 ##.Plodder.F←##.FilesAndDirs                       ⍝ so it must be established here

 :For logFolder :In 'Logs1' 'Logs2/'
     g←⎕NS''
     g.INI←∆CreateIni'Test_Misc_007'('[LOGGING]' 'Log = 1'('Folder = ''',folder,'/',logFolder,''''))
     'CREATE!'##.FilesAndDirs.CheckPath folder,'/',logFolder
     g←##.Plodder.OpenAppLog g
     →T.PassesIf 2=g.⎕NC'AppLogTie'
     ⎕NUNTIE g.AppLogTie
     →T.PassesIf ⎕NEXISTS folder,'/',(logFolder~'/'),'/app-log.txt'
 :EndFor

 g←⎕NS''
 g.INI←∆CreateIni'Test_Misc_007'('[LOGGING]' 'Log = 0'('Folder = ''',folder,'/Logs'''))
 g←##.Plodder.OpenAppLog g
 →T.PassesIf 0=g.⎕NC'AppLogTie'

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
